      ":question/id": "151f6833-d48f-54c3-9386-a95df61d0703",
      ":question/problem": "Given that\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 11 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhich of the following elementary row operations makes $a_{33}=0$?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Of the given options, we consider the row operation\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nAt the requested entry, this gives\n\n$$\na_{33}=8+(-2)\\cdot (4)=0.\n$$\n\nApplying the above row operation, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A &=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 11 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\qquad {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ &\\sim \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 11 \\\\ -1 & 17 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-2){R}_{1}.\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
